// Bubali Bird Sanctuary wetland (Bubali Plas), the two connected sewage-fed ponds behind Eagle Beach and the Palm
// Beach strip. Off with ?bubali=0. A draws the whole spot as dry sand: the OSM ponds (relation 5638923, ~13 ha west
// pond, and way 79078396, ~10 ha north-east pond) are in the region data, but A only renders sea-level water.
// References (Commons CC0/CC BY-SA photos, satellite) show olive-grey still water edged by grey-brown mud, tall green
// reed/cattail walls with water-hyacinth mats, dense green mangrove-like thicket between the ponds and dry cunucu
// scrub round them, with egrets and herons on the margins. Rebuilt in code from OSM geometry; photos are reference only.
// 4 draw calls, built once (over a few timer ticks) when the regions under it have heights, no per-frame work beyond a
// night tint: one vertex-coloured sheet (pond water, mud rim and two-sided reed-bed walls), and three InstancedMeshes
// sharing one material (reed tufts, thicket/scrub clumps, egret specks). Low gets coarser water cells and fewer clumps.
// Kept clear: A's roads (half width + 3 m) and buildings, the Bubali lookout tower and its board (30 m), and 4 m cells
// already used by other places' models (J.E. Irausquin fofoti and boulders, Noord street walls, fill houses).
